  "_comment": [
    "Keyword sweep lexicon (plan v3 section 4). Every entry: display form -> extra spelling variants.",
    "The display form itself is always matched. Matching is case-insensitive with tech-aware word",
    "boundaries (C++, C#, Node.js, CI/CD survive), longest variant first; a matched span is consumed",
    "so 'Azure OpenAI' does not also yield 'Azure'. Entries listed under case_sensitive only match",
    "with the exact casing shown (AI, ML, KI, SAP, Excel, Go, Swift); single-letter languages",
    "(R, C) additionally need list context (comma, slash, parenthesis or 'and'/'or' neighbours).",
    "german: German JD term -> English equivalent; German ads print 'Datenanalyse (Data Analysis)'.",
    "Extend this file when a real JD keyword is missed - no code changes needed."
